from 1038 and 1209), so ignoring time would suggest a link; the traversal tool does recover a valid \u2264600 route 1209->883 at t=73318, proving the negative result is real; 1010's upstream partner 1429 likewise cannot reach 883; and 1010's only outgoing edges occur outside this window."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion:** No time-respecting cascade exists.\n\n- Node 1010 has exactly **one** event in the window and it is **incoming** (1429 \u2192 1010, step_09/step_03/step_04): it never sends anything, so no cascade can originate from it.\n- Constrained (\u2264600) temporal reachability from 1010 reaches only itself (step_01); no paths enumerated (step_12).\n- **Confounder controls:** (a) even with *no* wait limit, 1010 cannot reach 883 (step_06) \u2014 so this is not a \"gap too long\" artifact but a directed-orientation failure; (b) the static k-hop neighbourhood is large and 883 does have in-contacts 1038/1209 (step_05, step_07), i.e. time-ignoring connectivity/volume would mislead; (c) the traversal machinery does find genuine \u2264600 routes into 883 from 1209 at t=73318 (step_13), so the negative is not a tool failure; (d) 1010's only in-partner 1429 also cannot reach 883 (step_14); (e) 1010's out-edges exist only *outside* this window (step_15), confirming the window, not the graph, excludes it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Within [51317, 89717] node 1010 participates in a single interaction, and it is inbound (1429->1010). With zero outgoing events there is no first hop for a cascade, so the \u2264600-unit time-respecting search from 1010 reaches only itself and enumerates no paths. This is not merely a waiting-time violation: unconstrained temporal reachability also fails, showing the barrier is directional/temporal orientation rather than gap length. Alternative explanations were tested and rejected: the static neighbourhood around 1010 is large and 883 does receive contacts (from 1038 and 1209), so ignoring time would suggest a link; the traversal tool does recover a valid \u2264600 route 1209->883 at t=73318, proving the negative result is real; 1010's upstream partner 1429 likewise cannot reach 883; and 1010's only outgoing edges occur outside this window.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 56630, "total_output_tokens": 4030, "total_tokens": 60660, "total_latency_ms": 60869, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}